{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520583-nosferatu-warren-depth-and-scope","id":1520583,"title":"Nosferatu Warren Depth and Scope","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-14T03:59:44-07:00","id":1520583,"title":"Nosferatu Warren Depth and Scope","content":"I've was messing around with an expansive warren design when I realized there wasn't really a depth restriction for the Nosferatu. We often think of the Nosferatu as just living in sewer systems or existing cave systems and occasionally expanding them, but with access to Potence, Animalism, and super mutant animal Ghouls.... they could get some real depth in relatively little time.<br /> <br /> The deepest levels of the mine/warren might be well over 130 degrees due to ambient geothermal heat around 1000 feet below the surface, but unless it causes ignition heat doesn't bother a vampire. Some levels might be flooded with water, but once again that wouldn't bother a vampire, nor would it matter if the bottom most levels didn't have proper air ventilation since they don't need air to breath and the stale or useless gasses would function for allowing speech to occur.<br /> <br /> At the 75 to 100 feet below surface mark, you won't be running into building foundations or sewer lines and won't threaten the stability of even a large building. So then other than some difficult types of geology to dig through or functionally brace, what exactly would restrict or contain a Warrens depth, overall width, or population?<br /> <br /> The only thing I could think of was access to blood. But even then, it is less of an issue than it would be for other clans. Thanks to Animalism the Elders could sate their appetite on animal blood. The intermediary levels of the Warren could be developed for human/animal herd residence, after a generation or two underground the knowledge of the surface will fade into myth or be forgotten entirely. The weak point is feeding the human or animal herds but depending on how you run the effects of nosferatu blood mutation and the viability of creating cave fisheries, only minimal supplies would need to be brought in from the surface.<br /> <br /> Beyond the supply issue, most of what could threaten this sort of Deep Warren seems to be Deus Ex Machina grade stuff, the Nictuku, sleeping eldritch entities the Baali worship, Elemental spirits from the deep umbra, etc.<br /> <br /> Trying to attack such a Deep Warren also presents interesting challenges. You can't just try to seal the surface access point because the occupants either have several or can dig new ones. At that depth you can't make changes to a city sewer system to restrict them, nor could you functionally get mining equipment in place to dig them out in a hidden way that the Nosferatu wouldn't see coming or just straight up break the masquerade in the attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T05:16:11-07:00","id":1520585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520583-nosferatu-warren-depth-and-scope#post1520583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I could think of was access to blood. But even then, it is less of an issue than it would be for other clans. Thanks to Animalism the Elders could sate their appetite on animal blood. The intermediary levels of the Warren could be developed for human/animal herd residence, after a generation or two underground the knowledge of the surface will fade into myth or be forgotten entirely. The weak point is feeding the human or animal herds but depending on how you run the effects of nosferatu blood mutation and the viability of creating cave fisheries, only minimal supplies would need to be brought in from the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall reading somewhere that cave biospheres are pretty delicate, so it's probably not as easy as setting up a spawning pool if you want to maintain it long term. And while natural dangers like ground gas aren't a problem for the undead, it is for livestock.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger issue for Nosferatu in particular is that access to mortal infrastructure gets more difficult the deeper you go. You can route electricity down to some depth, but even that gets a challenge that would need some serious planning and engineering. But more relevant would probably be the difficulty of 'commuting' to the surface. The good thing about sewer level warrens or thereabout is that it is still relatively close to the social resources that Nosferatu employ.<br /> <br /> Deep warrens like that would be excellent safe houses though, and good locations for archives or similar. It's a good place for elders to sleep undisturbed for a long time, so instead of an eldritch monstrosity it's perhaps more likely a trespasser could be confronted with a hungry elder. 'Digging too deep' is good story trope though, so it doesn't have to be mutually exclusive.<br /> There's another risk in the form of cave-ins. Tectonic shifts happen all the time. I recall news about agencies having 'lost' the location of caverns where nuclear waste was stored, simply because the cavern was now solid rock.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T06:15:38-07:00","id":1520587,"title":"","content":"In addition to the psychological factor, which is that you have to stay in a buried and perhaps even isolated place, the animals part would be complicated with rats or rabbits, if my memory fails, you would need to feed on four of them to get just one blood point . Other than putting kindreds alone and isolated in one place for so long is asking them to do stupid things. If you find it interesting you could explore the problem of black mold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T12:17:02-07:00","id":1520603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520583-nosferatu-warren-depth-and-scope?p=1520585#post1520585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Digging too deep' is good story trope though</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone is gangsta until they bump in to a Vhujunka outpost/city whily diggin' too deep...<br /> It is bad enough a Nosferatu warren could potentially hit a K'llasshaa\u200b &quot;Temple&quot;, an undergrond sea full of Chluroviah, Wichtel or goblin community or a Black Spiral tunel (or a Thunderwyrm decide to turn left at Albuquerque and ends up in the middle of the nest) but there are worse things down there that would make a Balrog hide under its bed (actually the Nameless Things are just that in Tolkien's work, Gandalf and the Balrog decided okay, time to get the hell out of their lair)\u200b<br /> Tho' I think even non-sabbat Nosferatu warrens make a deal or two with the Dancers to share property<br /> Especially with the Hives that follow The Dark Fungus, &quot;His Mycological Majesty&quot;\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T12:53:03-07:00","id":1520607,"title":"","content":"Another thing is that at some point, things just get too inconvenient. While Nosferatu (like all vampires) are monsters, they are not monsters that evolved naturally to make the underground their natural habitat. It is a very unnatural environment. Simply because they can survive it, does not mean they want to live there anymore than coal miners want to live in coal mines. They'll want easy egress to the surface to feed on humans, ample room so they can stand up straight, stay in touch with mortal and Kindred society, enjoy the sights, sounds, and smells of the surface world. Yes, we say Nosferatu build their warrens in sewers, but how many Nosferatu actually prefer to live in that filth as opposed to having a safehouse? How many want to live in D&amp;D style dungeons/tunnels for all their existence?<br /> <br /> While the Nosferatu warren in the sewer is an interesting trope, for most of the existence of the Nosferatu there was nothing like a modern sewer system. Only a few great cities had anything like that. Most Nosferatu, historically, probably never lived in sewers or in deep underground caverns. They got by without it.<br /> <br /> Also, at some point the amount of excavation begins to attract attention rather than providing safety and anonymity. Where do you place all this earth and rock you are removing? What happens if it collapses on you? What if it causes some sort of seismic anomaly and surface scientists determine there is some honeycomb down there that is unexplained? After a certain point of digging, I think the negatives outweigh the benefits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jKVDdMG37ig\" data-code=\"jKVDdMG37ig\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jKVDdMG37ig/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520583-nosferatu-warren-depth-and-scope?p=1520603#post1520603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone is gangsta until they bump in to a Vhujunka outpost/city whily diggin' too deep...</div> </div> </div> </div>For an ST who has mastered the other gamelines, there are certainly a lot of things an ST can put down there. Besides actual physical chambers occupied by various creatures of the Wyrm, at some point the Gauntlet likely drops to real low and all sorts of umbral critters can flow out of an Umbral domain that coexists with the material. You can have Nocker miners in the Dreaming that cross over. Plasmic entities. Or hiding places of Nephandi horrors. It's just a manner of figuring out what sort of things add to a Vampire game, and which would distract from it.<br /> <br /> When I only played Vampire, I didn't want to think about such things because they often get in the way of the themes and mood of Vampire. But I'm now much more willing to include other gameline elements to present a chronicle setting which is vampire focused, but acknowledges other supernatural creatures. I think that adds to the setting. But I do think it can be a challenge to find the appropriate implementation that complements Vampire (and the expectations and enjoyment of the players) rather than detracting from it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T13:13:21-07:00","id":1520608,"title":"","content":"Depending on how canonical you treat the contents of <i>Gehenna</i>, it's also possible that the Gangrel Antediluvian earth-melded as a wandering genius loci is another risk of digging down too low. Whatever it uses to navigate and detect prey down there, I bet a warren of Nosferatu holed up half a mile down ping a lot louder than the diffuse blanket of nematodes and microorganisms that normally make up the life at that depth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T15:11:11-07:00","id":1520617,"title":"","content":"I found that implied threats work best with the already intense psychological pressure you can create with underground adventures. Think about how the single Xenomorph in the original Alien added so much tension with getting only minimal screen time. It's the catalyst that amplifies the natural fear induced by an isolated environment that by itself threatens death by simply being in there. The minds of the players are always better at filling in paranoia than any ST can provide with narrative, imo. If you leave the Big Bad Hunting Thing a nebulous entity and only hint at its presence through environmental storytelling, players will fill in the blanks with their personal nemeses and phobias.<br /> <br /> I had a few very cool sessions in which I sent my troupe down abandoned (and magically twisted) subway tunnels which had become the nest of rat spirits, just hinting at their presence through debris and glimpses at the edge of the character's vision at times. Small beady eyes, always watching. By the time they arrived at their goal, the whole troupe was convinced they were completely at the mercy of the swarm, trapped miles below the surface. It's really good horror if you can keep up the mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}